    "The glass was too thick to transmit light"
  ],
  "answer": 0,
  "why": "Daylight is a flux to be admitted deliberately: glare and heat force the blinds, so the building delivers worse daylight AND a worse energy bill than a modest, well-oriented window would have."
};

const edDaylightCloze = {
  "text": "Daylight penetrates roughly %%0%% times the window-head height — a 3 m head gives %%1%% m of usable depth — and the %%2%% reflects high-angle sun onto the ceiling to push the bright zone deeper while shading the desk.",
  "answers": [
    [
      "2 to 2.5",
      "2–2.5",
      "2.5",
      "two to two and a half"
    ],
    [
      "6–7.5",
      "6 to 7.5"
    ],
    [
      "light shelf",
      "light-shelf"
    ]
  ],
